{
  "$comment": "Golden vectors for @libriant/shared/greek. Read greek.ts before changing anything here.\n\nTWO KINDS OF VECTOR, and the difference matters:\n\n  named*  — hand-specified and hand-verified. These assert that the fold is\n            CORRECT. Changing one is a claim about Greek, not about code.\n  sweep   — generated from the TypeScript implementation over the Greek,\n            Greek Extended and Latin supplement blocks. These assert only\n            that every runtime computes the SAME thing, which is the only\n            property a second implementation can be held to. They are what\n            check:greek-folding runs through Postgres today, and what the\n            OpenSearch analyzer (phase 82) and the Rust core (phase 77) will\n            be held to later.\n\nA divergence here is never fixed by editing the expected value. Fix the\nimplementation that disagrees, or change every implementation together.",
  "namedFold": [
    {
      "in": "ΠΟΛΙΣ",
      "out": "πολισ",
      "why": "the defect: JS toLowerCase gives final sigma U+03C2, a typist gives U+03C3"
    },
    {
      "in": "πολισ",
      "out": "πολισ",
      "why": "what a person actually types"
    },
    {
      "in": "πόλις",
      "out": "πολισ",
      "why": "accented, written form"
    },
    {
      "in": "Η ΠΟΛΙΣ ΕΑΛΩ",
      "out": "η πολισ εαλω",
      "why": "a real title catalogued in capitals"
    },
    {
      "in": "ΣΟΦΟΣ",
      "out": "σοφοσ",
      "why": "both sigmas collapse"
    },
    {
      "in": "ΎΔΩΡ",
      "out": "υδωρ",
      "why": "U+038E: the database default collation folded this to omega"
    },
    {
      "in": "Ώρα",
      "out": "ωρα",
      "why": "U+038F: the database default collation folded this to U+03CF"
    },
    {
      "in": "ᾍ",
      "out": "α",
      "why": "polytonic: dasia + oxia + ypogegrammeni all inside U+0300-U+036F"
    },
    {
      "in": "ᾳ",
      "out": "α",
      "why": "iota subscript U+0345 is inside the combining range"
    },
    {
      "in": "ᾷ",
      "out": "α",
      "why": "perispomeni + ypogegrammeni"
    },
    {
      "in": "ΐ",
      "out": "ι",
      "why": "dialytika + tonos"
    },
    {
      "in": "ΰ",
      "out": "υ",
      "why": "dialytika + tonos on upsilon"
    },
    {
      "in": "Ϲοφια",
      "out": "σοφια",
      "why": "lunate sigma capital U+03F9"
    },
    {
      "in": "ϲοφια",
      "out": "σοφια",
      "why": "lunate sigma small U+03F2"
    },
    {
